#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078350 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078498 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45915032-87ea-583d-8570-ad1d56d019b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Cube Given a Side Length"}] :question/id #uuid "d27805b4-9ade-5429-b5d9-85f202750d97" :question/math-academy-id "e-7150" :question/problem "![](images/2e/2ea953a445de3655c3977cffcc3e5834cae936508cbbee761988b0f71d99a50c.png)\n\nDetermine the surface area for the cube above." :question/worked-solution "The surface area $S$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nS = 6s^2\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\ns = 7\\,\\textrm{m}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we get\n\n$$\nS = 6(7\\, \\text{m})^2 = 294\\,\\textrm{m}^2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078351 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078499 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "676d79a5-129d-5e14-ad1f-4af43090459f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Side Length of a Cube Given the Surface Area"}] :question/id #uuid "1572978d-d8a9-5a85-b5f7-dc724de52824" :question/math-academy-id "e-7151" :question/problem "The surface area of a cube is $240$ square units. Find the length of the edges of the cube." :question/worked-solution "The surface area $S$ of a cube is made of $6$ congruent squares. So, the area $\\mathcal A$ of one face is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac{S}{6} = \\frac{240}{6} = 40\\,\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A = s^2\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns = \\sqrt{\\mathcal{A}} = \\sqrt{40} = 2\\sqrt{10}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $2\\sqrt{10}$ units."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078376 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078523 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b01e7b76-466f-522d-bfd1-aa8616cbe023" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Lateral Surface Area of a Cube Given its Dimensions"}] :question/id #uuid "80eb6640-3bd6-5cff-81c5-7e6b850d6f93" :question/math-academy-id "e-9015" :question/problem "![](images/8b/8bbdcdc749ecf9bf1a2aae1904f7be960139be55df49f5a23c1b657656df0f7d.png)\n\nDetermine the lateral surface area for the cube above." :question/worked-solution "The lateral surface area $S_L$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nS_L = 4s^2\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\ns = 9\\,\\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we get\n\n$$\nS_L = 4(9\\, \\text{cm})^2 = 324 \\,\\textrm{cm}^2\n$$"}]}
